{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Pharaoh named [Bb]him Za-phen-ath-pa-neah
Gave [Eb]him Asen[Gm]ath, daughter of [F]Potiphera
Priest of [Eb]On, a [Gm]wife of grace
Joseph stood be[F]fore the king
Thirty years old in [Bb]that land
He [F]left the palace, trav[Gm]eled on
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
May [Bb]God make you like [F]Ephraim and [Gm]Manasseh
[Eb]Blessed with names [F]that carry [Gm]on
In[Eb]heritance equal, [F]sons of Is[Bb]rael
Adopted in the covenant [Eb]home
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Be[Bb]fore the famine came to [Eb]pass
Two [Gm]sons were born in [F]the land
Manas[Eb]seh, the firstborn [Gm]son
God made him for[F]get his hardship
Ephraim, the [Eb]fruitful boy
[Gm]Born where he had suffered [F]long
Asenath, mother of these two
Se[Bb]cured their place [F]in the genealo[Gm]gy
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
May [Bb]God make you [F]like Ephraim [Gm]and Manas[Eb]seh
Blessed with [F]names that carry [Gm]on
In[Eb]heritance equal, [F]sons of Is[Bb]rael
[Eb]Adopted in the cove[F]nant home
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Ja[Gm]cob sat up on his bed
[Bb]Saw his face again at [Eb]last
Took the boys to his heart
Crossed his [F]hands in blessing
Right hand [Gm]on the younger [Eb]head
Left hand on the firstborn son
I know, my son, I [Bb]know
The y[F]ounger will be greater
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Gm]May God make [Bb]you like Ephraim [F]and Manas[Gm]seh
Blessed with names [Eb]that carry [F]on
Inheri[Gm]tance equal, sons [Eb]of Israel
Adop[F]ted in the co[Bb]venant home
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
So [Eb]he put Ephraim [F]ahead
Of [Eb]Manasseh, the first[Bb]born
{end_of_verse}

